==Tenure==

===The "Winter of Discontent" (January–February 2026)===
{{main|En Crisis}}
The coalition faced its first major crisis in early 2026, dubbed by the media as the "{{Nihongo|Winter of Discontent|不満の冬|Fuman no Fuyu}}." The {{Nihongo|"En Crisis"|円危機|En Kiki}}—a sharp 20% depreciation of the Sanese currency—accelerated in late January, driving up the cost of imported energy and staples. Minister of Health Nakayama publicly demanded an emergency "Inflation Relief Package" worth 5 trillion [[Sanese En]], threatening that the OSP would boycott the FY2026 budget vote if these demands were not met. The standoff was resolved on February 24 through a "Triple Bind" agreement, but the compromise alienated both the PPO's business base and the OSP's progressive activists.

===The March Maelstrom===
{{main|Nakayama Station dragging incident}}
On March 1, 2026, 17-year-old student {{nihongo|Yamamoto Hina|山本日奈}} was killed by a one-man operated train on the OR Okayama Line. Honda's initial response—defending the one-man operation mandate as economically vital—was widely interpreted as prioritizing corporate efficiency over human life. When leaked video evidence showed the driver distracted by a company-issued iPhone linked to Honda's Digital Rail Initiative, the resulting {{Nihongo|Mirror Yoshi protest movement|鏡よし運動|Kagami Yoshi Undō}} saw hand-drawn mirrors affixed to PPO offices across Okaiken.

On March 9, a televised standoff between Honda and Minister Nakayama resulted in Nakayama publicly clearing his office, signaling the functional end of the coalition. By March 11, the Honda government was reduced to minority status following the formal withdrawal of the OSP. On March 12, the LDP successfully passed a motion of no confidence, triggering the dissolution of the House of Commoners and scheduling the snap election for 17 May 2026.

===The Satori AI Blackout Crisis (May 1–4, 2026)===
{{main|Satori AI Blackout Crisis}}
Sixteen days before the election, the [[Satori AI]] grid experienced a catastrophic cascade failure, paralysing the nation for 72 hours. The crisis claimed 23 lives and caused an estimated ¥4.2 trillion in economic damage. The Blackout retrospectively validated every position the opposition had argued against the cabinet's digital modernization agenda. On May 8, the Adonian Credit Transparency Agency (ACTA) issued a historic downgrade of Okaiken's sovereign credit rating from 5 stars to 3 stars.

==Defeated ministers==
The 2026 election was unusually punishing to sitting cabinet ministers, with six of the sixteen members losing their constituencies to opposition challengers—a rate of ministerial defeat without precedent in modern Sanese electoral history.

