==Legacy==
The Honda-Nakayama Cabinet is widely regarded as one of the most consequential failed governments in modern Sanese political history. Its collapse—triggered by the intersection of the En Crisis, the Nakayama Station incident, and the Satori Blackout—fundamentally realigned the Sanese political landscape, ending the PPO's decades-long dominance and paving the way for the [[Ikazaki Cabinet]].

Political analysts have identified three structural failures of the cabinet: the inability to reconcile the PPO's technocratic fiscal conservatism with the OSP's democratic socialist platform; the over-reliance on digital modernization as a governance philosophy without adequate safety redundancy; and the failure to recognise that the coalition's 231-seat minority position required genuine compromise rather than procedural management.

